	"_doc": "Who the humanoid rig can field. 'themes' gives each theme a grunt, a rusher and a heavy: one of 'characters' is picked at random for each enemy, it carries the model scenes/models/<weapon> or nothing, moves with the 'default' or the 'zombie' set, and 'tuning' is written over the exported variables of scripts/enemy.gd (a pair such as cooldown is [shortest, longest]; eye_height and head_start are the mean of the role's characters, each character's own are in its line). 'characters' has a line per character, written by tools/import_character.sh: where it came from and under what licence, and for a placeholder why it is one and what should replace it ('wanted' is a prompt for that). tools/characters/build_cast.sh builds them all again; assets/characters/sheets/<id>.jpg shows each.",
